  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "dog is mapped as 'her' in the text",
  "description": "The text 'you can't get her pregnant if she's a goat' uses the word 'her' to refer to the dog in the image. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity (the dog) is being mapped onto the textual pronoun 'her', establishing the dog as the subject of the statement. The humor relies on this mapping, as the dog is visually presented as a female entity (implied by 'her') despite being a dog, and the text plays on the biological impossibility of a dog being a 'goat' (a male goat or a desirable person) to create absurdity.",
